## Dev loop

This repo came out of generation already fully set up — `uv sync` and `inv configure` (venv,
`direnv allow`, the Claude Code Bash-tool hook, and the canonical `ruff.toml`/`pyrightconfig.json`/
`dprint.json`/`pytest.ini`/`.editorconfig` from [`repo-tasks`](https://github.com/TheodoreAD/repo-tasks))
already ran automatically at generation time. Day to day:

- `inv quality.precommit` before considering a change done — fixes what's auto-fixable, then runs the
  full check gate. See `repo-tasks` for what each step does, and how new task modules show up under
  their own prefix automatically as `repo-tasks` grows, with no change needed here.
- `pytest` — tests live in `tests/`, fixture-based, no live network calls.
- `inv configure` again any time — safe to re-run, e.g. after `uv sync` picks up new dependencies, or
  to re-pull the latest canonical config once `repo-tasks` is bumped
  (`uv lock --upgrade-package repo-tasks`).
{% if with_docs -%}
- `inv docs.build` builds the docs site (zensical, strict mode) to `site/`; `inv docs.serve` runs it
  locally with live reload. `.github/workflows/docs.yml` deploys it to GitHub Pages automatically on
  every push to `main` — **publicly**, even if this repo itself is private.
{% endif %}
{% if interface == "mcp_server" -%}
## Installation

Add a stable `PATH` binary via `uv tool`, then register it with Claude Code:

```shell
# while actively developing (editable, picks up local edits):
uv tool install -e ~/projects/github.com-personal/{{ package_name.replace('_', '-') }}

# once not actively iterating, from GitHub instead:
uv tool install git+https://github.com/{{ github_repo }}

# either way, registration is the same one-liner:
claude mcp add --scope user {{ package_name }} {{ package_name }}
```

`--scope user` makes the server available in every project on this machine. See
[`mcp-skill-shipping`](https://github.com/TheodoreAD/power-user-linux-setup/blob/master/skills/mcp-skill-shipping/SKILL.md)
for the full pattern (project-scope alternative, switching install sources, etc.).
{% elif interface == "skill" -%}
## Installation

Skills ship via the existing `inv ai.skills` mechanism — no per-repo install step. Once this repo is
public with a real skill directory, add it to a `power-user-linux-setup` `setup.toml` package:

```toml
skills = [{ source = "npx", repo = "{{ github_repo }}" }]
```

then `inv ai.skills` makes it available globally, same as every other declared skill.
